# App-authored transition, not from a tape. No tape or manual in the library
# reaches Focus 11. The only descriptive footing is the unverified secondary
# overview at library/reference/focus-levels-overview.md; this body labels that
# footing aloud and makes no claim about what the transition should feel like.

@segment    climb-f10-f11
@title      Climb — Focus 10 to Focus 11
@levels     F11
@from       F10
@fixed
@verbosity  3
@protected  Focus 11
@duration   ~55s

say From Focus 10, you will move one step to Focus 11.
pause 4
say The only available map is a secondary overview. It calls Focus 11 the Access Channel, but no tape or manual here establishes what the transition should feel like.
pause 6
say Let the number mark the change, and let your own observation supply the account.
pause 5
level F11
say Ten.
pause 5
say Eleven.
pause 8
